.\" amiscan(1) - Amiga virus scanner
.TH AMISCAN 1 "2026-10-12" "AmiScan 0.1b1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
amiscan \- check Amiga files, disk images and archives for Amiga viruses
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amiscan
.RI [ options ]
.IR file | folder " ..."
.br
.B amiscan \-update
.RB [ \-force ]
.br
.B amiscan \-version
.br
.B amiscan \-list
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amiscan
looks for Amiga viruses \(em boot block viruses, file viruses, link viruses
and data viruses \(em in files, folders, Amiga disk images and archives.
.PP
It does not imitate a virus checker: it runs the Amiga's own virus database,
.BR xvs.library ,
the one VirusZ\~III, VirusExecutor and VirusChecker\~II use, unchanged, in a
68020 processor and a small AmigaOS built into the program.
.PP
Disk images (ADF, ADZ, DMS, HDF) and archives (LhA, LZX, Zip, 7z, RAR, ARJ,
ARC, ZOO, CAB, tar, gzip, bzip2, xz) are recognised by their contents, not
their names, and opened, also inside each other. Packed programs and data
(PowerPacker, Imploder, StoneCracker, CrunchMania, XPK and about a hundred
more) are unpacked with
.B xfdmaster.library
and
.BR xpkmaster.library .
Every file found this way, and every floppy's boot block, is checked. Boot
blocks also get a second opinion from the
.I Amiga Bootblock Reader
database, which names harmless boot blocks and knows some boot viruses
xvs.library does not.
.PP
None of these databases and libraries is part of AmiScan.
.B amiscan \-update
downloads them from where their authors publish them (see
.BR PARTS ).
.SH OPTIONS
Options may come before or after the file names;
.B \-\-
ends them.
.SS What to check
.TP
.BI \-libs " folder"
Use the parts in
.I folder
instead of the default (see
.BR FILES ).
.TP
.BI \-max " size"
The biggest file checked or unpacked into, like
.BR 300M " or " 1.5G
(default 1536M, the most). Memory use is about twice this at most. A bigger
file is reported as not checked; if it is not an archive or disk image it is
not even read.
.TP
.BI \-max\-total " size"
How much one file on disk may unpack to in all, and how big an archive or
disk image may itself be (default 8G). Archives and disk images are read into
memory whole.
.SS What to report
.TP
.BI \-show " kinds"
Which results the report lists, separated by commas:
.BR virus ", " damaged ", " unchecked ", " clean ,
or
.BR all " or " none .
Default:
.BR virus,damaged,unchecked .
.TP
.B \-v
List the clean files too (\fB\-show all\fR).
.TP
.B \-q
Only the summary line (\fB\-show none\fR).
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Write the report to
.I file
instead of the terminal, which then gets only the summary. The extension
picks the format:
.BR .txt " text, " .md " Markdown, " .html " a web page, " .json " JSON."
.TP
.BI \-format " format"
.BR text ", " markdown ", " html ", " json " or " bbs ,
whatever the extension of
.B \-o
says.
.TP
.B \-bbs
One line per file, for BBS software (see
.BR "BBS USE" ).
.TP
.B \-json
One JSON object per file and boot block checked, then a summary object.
.SS Other
.TP
.B \-update
Download the newest parts (see
.BR PARTS ).
Only what changed since the last time is fetched. A new part replaces the
old one only after it has been tried: it must load and pass its own test,
must not be older, and xvs.library must carry Georg Wittmann's signature.
The old files are kept in
.IR libs/old/ ,
the archives as published in
.IR libs/archives/ .
.TP
.B \-force
With
.BR \-update :
download even when nothing changed.
.TP
.B \-version
Show the version of AmiScan and of each part, and which are missing.
.TP
.B \-list
List every virus xvs.library knows, by kind.
.TP
.B \-trace
Log every call the Amiga code makes to the built-in AmigaOS (for debugging).
.SH THE REPORT
At the end
.B amiscan
lists, grouped by the file on disk, with where inside it and why:
.TP
.B Viruses
the virus name and kind (boot, file, link or data virus).
.TP
.B Damaged
archive members that are broken (a CRC error, data that ends early) and
packed programs whose packed data is broken. They are checked as far as they
unpack, which is what LhA itself would write out. An archive entry that
holds nothing at all (one byte value repeated, as in the fake entries BBS
adverts are made of) counts as clean.
.TP
.B Not checked
what could not be checked, and why: a password, a missing part, a size
limit.
.PP
A file unpacked from a packed one appears as
.IR "name (unpacked PowerPacker 4.0)" .
.SH BBS USE
Amiga BBS software ran a file checker on every upload.
.B amiscan \-bbs
prints one line per file in that spirit:
.PP
.RS
.nf
0 UPLOAD.LHA is clean
1 UPLOAD.LHA is infected with Amixhack, BossNuke 1.5\(ss
2 UPLOAD.LHA is corrupted: docs/readme: lha: CRC mismatch
3 UPLOAD.LHA could not be checked: the file itself (packed contents): XPK Crypted needs a password to unpack
.fi
.RE
.PP
A file with several problems gets the worst: a virus, then corrupted, then
could not be checked. Software can use the number, the words (AmiExpress
failed an upload when the checker's output held one of the sysop's words),
or the exit status, which is the same number. For uploads from strangers,
limit memory, for example
.BR "\-max 300M \-max\-total 1G" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
The worst result over all files:
.TP
.B 0
nothing found
.TP
.B 1
a virus
.TP
.B 2
a damaged file or archive
.TP
.B 3
something could not be checked; also when
.B amiscan
itself cannot run (no xvs.library, a bad option, a failed update).
.SH PARTS
.TP
.B xvs.library
the virus database, by Georg Wittmann, from the Virus Help Team,
.UR https://www.vht\-dk.dk/amiga/xvs/xvs.htm
.UE .
Needed.
.TP
.BR xfdmaster.library " and " xfd/
unpack packed programs; by Georg H\(:ormann and Dirk St\(:ocker, from Aminet
(util/pack/xfdmaster.lha). Recommended.
.TP
.BR xpkmaster.library " and " compressors/
unpack XPK files; by Dirk St\(:ocker and others, from Aminet
(util/pack/xpk_User.lha). Recommended.
.TP
.B abr\-brainfile.xml, abr\-searchbrain.xml
the boot block database of Amiga Bootblock Reader by Jason and Jordan Smith,
from its GitHub repository. Recommended.
.PP
Without the recommended parts
.B amiscan
still runs, but checks less;
.B \-version
shows what is missing.
.SH FILES
The parts folder, the first that holds xvs.library of:
.TP
.BI \-libs " folder"
.TP
.B $AMISCAN_LIBS
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/amiscan/libs
on Linux (or
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/amiscan/libs );
.I %AppData%\eAmiScan\elibs
on Windows;
.I ~/Library/Application Support/AmiScan/libs
on macOS
.TP
.I libs/
next to the
.B amiscan
program
.TP
.IR /usr/local/share/amiscan/libs ", " /usr/share/amiscan/libs
.PP
.B \-update
writes to the folder in use, or else the third one.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AMISCAN_LIBS
the parts folder.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
on Linux, where the parts folder is by default.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B amiscan \-update
Install or update the parts.
.TP
.B amiscan ~/Downloads
Check a folder and list what was found.
.TP
.B amiscan \-o report.html ~/Amiga
Save the report as a web page.
.TP
.B amiscan \-bbs \-max 300M \-max\-total 1G upload.lha
Check an upload for a BBS.
.TP
.B amiscan \-show virus \-q game.adf; echo $?
Only the summary, and the exit status.
.SH SAFETY
The Amiga code runs inside
.BR amiscan 's
own emulated Amiga. It can read its parts folder and nothing else on the
computer, and it never runs the files being checked: those are only data
handed to the virus database. Every call into the Amiga code has a time limit,
and a crash in it becomes an error, not a crashed program.
.SH LIMITS
Files packed with a password cannot be unpacked; they are reported as not
checked. Very new or rare packers that xfdmaster and XPK do not know are
checked only as they are.
